From: Codex <codex@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] user32: DrawText's DT_PREFIXONLY in the external shell

Purpose: draw the Windows 7 Start menu's places (Control Panel, Help and
Support) once, as on Windows 7.
Windows behavior: with DT_PREFIXONLY, DrawText draws only the underscore
under the prefixed character, not the text. Windows 7's comctl32 list
view draws its labels and then calls DrawThemeTextEx with DT_PREFIXONLY
for the underscore.
Wine before: DT_PREFIXONLY was ignored, so those labels were drawn a
second time over themselves and looked bold (ClearType blended twice).
Change: in the external shell, skip ExtTextOut when DT_PREFIXONLY is set
and keep the underscore.
Evidence: the labels' pixels match Windows 7's in the Start menu
(coverage 43/255 stays 43/255 instead of 1-(1-a)^2).
Scope: the opted-in external shell; plain Wine is unchanged.
---
 dlls/user32/text.c | 5 ++++-
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/dlls/user32/text.c b/dlls/user32/text.c
index ede816e..2d8834d 100644
--- a/dlls/user32/text.c
+++ b/dlls/user32/text.c
@@ -1075,7 +1075,10 @@ INT WINAPI DrawTextExW( HDC hdc, LPWSTR str, INT i_count,
                 else
                     len_seg = len;
 
-                if (!ExtTextOutW( hdc, xseg, y,
+                /* DT_PREFIXONLY: only the underscore (Windows 7's list views
+                 * draw their labels, then ask for the underscore this way) */
+                if (!((flags & DT_PREFIXONLY) && win4wine_external_shell()) &&
+                    !ExtTextOutW( hdc, xseg, y,
                                  ((flags & DT_NOCLIP) ? 0 : ETO_CLIPPED) |
                                  ((flags & DT_RTLREADING) ? ETO_RTLREADING : 0),
                                  rect, str, len_seg, NULL ))
